<title>SINGAPORE: CWT 1996 net profit rises 10 pct.</title>
<headline>CWT 1996 net profit rises 10 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended Dec 31, 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of Singapore dollar unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			   8.28    vs   7.52</p>
<p>    Group share (cents)		5.51    vs   5.01</p>
<p>    Group share (fully diluted)    5.03    vs   4.78</p>
<p>    Dividend (cents)		   2.5     vs   2.5</p>
<p>    Turnover			   114.86    vs  78.23</p>
<p>    Interest income		    0.68    vs   0.31</p>
<p>    Interest expense		   1.03    vs   0.97</p>
<p>    Associates			   0.38    vs   0.48</p>
<p>    Pretax				13.06    vs  10.79</p>
<p>    Tax				    3.83    vs   2.69</p>
<p>    Minorities (loss)		  0.96    vs   0.59 (loss)</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries (loss)	  (1.10)   vs   nil</p>
<p>    Dividend pay		June 16</p>
<p>    Dividend register	 June 4</p>
<p>Note - CWT Distribution Ltd said its 1995 figures were adjusted to correct an overstatement of interest income and deferred taxation charge of Singapore $1.08 million and S$279,000 respectively.  </p>
<p>The company is involved in warehousing and logistics services, transportation services, port &amp; container freight station, engineering and container depot operations.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom 65-8703080</p>
</text>
